OL,3,ARecord heatwaves in France set to make
OL,4,Achampagne stronger
OL,5,
OL,6,FChampagne lovers may find themselves
OL,7,Fgetting tipsy more quickly after French
OL,8,Fproducers have been given the go-ahead
OL,9,Fto raise the alcohol content in a
OL,10,Fbottle of bubbly for the first time
OL,11,Ffollowing this summer's record
OL,12,Fheatwave.
OL,14,FWinemakers can temporarily produce
OL,15,Fchampagne with an alcohol content of up
OL,16,Fto 15% - above the 13% cap, industry
OL,17,Fofficials have said.
OL,19,FThe extreme heat and drought produced
OL,20,Fgrapes with exceptionally higher sugar
OL,21,Flevels. Yeast converts sugar into
OL,22,Falcohol during fermentation.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,318,300,200,140,0,100
